Third-party material and attribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This distribution contains no third-party code, scripts, binaries or
certificate files. It does not bundle repair scripts or compromised CA
certificates.

The indicator and remediation data in each skill's references/ directory
records facts (public key fingerprints, certificate authority names, fixed
package version strings, configuration patterns) transcribed by hand from the
public sources below. Each data file states its sources, retrieval dates,
"as of" dates and data version. The sources themselves are not redistributed;
only citations to them.

  * Mozilla Bugzilla bug 2083449 - "eMudhra: Weak keys in intermediate CA
    certificates"
    https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2083449
  * Google - "Protecting Chrome and Android users from compromised eMudhra
    intermediate CA certificates"
    https://blog.google/security/protecting-chrome-and-android-users-from-compromised-emudhra-intermediate-ca-certificates
  * eMudhra - "Certificate security incident"
    https://emudhra.com/en/post/certificate-security-incident
  * Cloudflare - "eMudhra certificate compromise"
    https://blog.cloudflare.com/emudhra-certificate-compromise
  * CISA - credential guidance
    https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/04/16/cisa-releases-guidance-credential-risks-associated-potential-legacy-oracle-cloud-compromise
    https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/analysis-reports/ar21-134a
  * Community advisory and remediation tracker
    https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/

